{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"ab08e2a3-2af7-4a62-9847-78394fa1e91b","step":{"id":"s1","script":"The rectangle represents every possible outcome. The circle is event A: the outcomes where A happens.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Complement of an event"},{"op":"figure","id":"venn","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-4.5,4.5],"y":[-3,3],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"polyline","id":"sample","points":[[-4,-2.5],[4,-2.5],[4,2.5],[-4,2.5]],"closed":true},{"kind":"text","at":[-3.6,2.1],"text":"S"},{"kind":"circle","id":"event","center":[-1,0],"r":1.5},{"kind":"text","at":[-1,0],"text":"A"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.warning","request_id":"ab08e2a3-2af7-4a62-9847-78394fa1e91b","code":"step_repaired","step_hint":"s2"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"ab08e2a3-2af7-4a62-9847-78394fa1e91b","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The complement of A contains everything inside the rectangle but outside the circle. It means A does not happen.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"outside","on":"venn","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[2,0.7],"text":"Aᶜ"},{"kind":"point","id":"outcome","at":[2,-0.7],"label":"not in A"},{"kind":"point","at":[-1,-0.7],"label":"in A"}]},{"op":"text","id":"definition","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"content":"The complement of A is the set of outcomes in S that are not in A."}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"ab08e2a3-2af7-4a62-9847-78394fa1e91b","step":{"id":"s3","script":"A and its complement never overlap, and together they include every outcome. Their probabilities therefore add to one.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"partition","on":"venn","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":[2,-1],"to":[2,-1.9],"arrow":true},{"kind":"text","at":[1.9,-2.15],"text":"the rest of S","size":"small"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"total","anchor":{"el":"definition","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"P(A)+P(A^c)=1"},{"op":"equation","id":"rule","anchor":{"el":"total","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"P(A^c)=1-P(A)"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"ab08e2a3-2af7-4a62-9847-78394fa1e91b","step":{"id":"s4","script":"If A has probability zero point three, its complement has probability zero point seven: all the probability left over.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"values","on":"venn","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[-1,0.65],"text":"0.3"},{"kind":"text","at":[2,1.3],"text":"0.7"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"example","anchor":{"el":"rule","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"P(A)=0.3\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad P(A^c)=1-0.3=0.7"}],"checkpoint":null}}
